{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.305, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 27, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:12.841Z", "t_ms": 5252, "delta": "**"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.455, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 28, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:12.987Z", "t_ms": 5398, "delta": "ReAct** (short for **Reasoning and Acting**) is a framework that"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.602, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:13.138Z", "t_ms": 5549, "delta": " enables large language models (LLMs) to generate both free-form reasoning traces (\"thoughts\") and task-specific actions in"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.826, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:13.349Z", "t_ms": 5760, "delta": " an interleaved manner [C1, C2]. \n\n### Core Concept and Mechanism\n* **Augmented Action Space:** ReAct extends"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.012, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:13.548Z", "t_ms": 5959, "delta": " an agent's standard action space ($\\mathcal{A}$) by combining it with the space of language ($\\mathcal{L}$)"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.153, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:13.688Z", "t_ms": 6099, "delta": " [C2]. Actions in the language space do not affect the external environment or yield observation feedback directly; instead, they"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.368, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:13.903Z", "t_ms": 6314, "delta": " serve as \"thoughts\" to compose information over the context and update it to guide subsequent reasoning and acting [C2]."}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.52, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:14.055Z", "t_ms": 6466, "delta": "\n* **Synergy Between Reasoning and Acting:** \n  * *Reasoning traces* allow the model to track progress, decompose"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.717, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:14.252Z", "t_ms": 6663, "delta": " goals, create and update action plans, incorporate commonsense knowledge, and handle exceptions [C1, C2].\n  "}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.895, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:14.428Z", "t_ms": 6839, "delta": "* *Actions* enable the model to interact with external environments or knowledge sources (such as APIs or search engines) to gather feedback and retrieve up"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.03, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:14.563Z", "t_ms": 6974, "delta": "-to-date observations [C1, C2].\n* **Execution Patterns:** For reasoning-heavy tasks ("}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.363, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:14.830Z", "t_ms": 7241, "delta": "e.g., question answering), generation alternates in a structured thought\u2013action\u2013observation loop [C3, C5]. For decision-"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.522, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:15.057Z", "t_ms": 7468, "delta": "making tasks involving many actions, thoughts can appear sparsely at key decision points [C3, C7].\n\n### Key"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.711, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 40, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:15.246Z", "t_ms": 7657, "delta": " Benefits\n* **Reduced Hallucination and Greater Grounding:** Interacting with external knowledge sources grounds the model in facts, substantially"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.873, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 41, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:15.408Z", "t_ms": 7819, "delta": " reducing the hallucination and error propagation typical of pure Chain-of-Thought (CoT) reasoning [C1, C5].\n"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.025, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 42, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:15.561Z", "t_ms": 7972, "delta": "* **Interpretability and Controllability:** ReAct produces human-like, step-by-step trajectories that humans can inspect for"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.222, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 43, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:15.753Z", "t_ms": 8164, "delta": " factual correctness or intervene in via thought editing to steer the model's behavior [C1, C3].\n* **Few-Shot"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.425, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 44, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:15.958Z", "t_ms": 8369, "delta": " Adaptation:** The framework can learn from just one to six in-context examples showing trajectories of thoughts, actions, and observations [C1"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.567, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 45, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:16.102Z", "t_ms": 8513, "delta": ", C3].\n\n### Applications and Performance\n* **Knowledge-Intensive Tasks:** Tested on HotpotQA (multi"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.792, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 46, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:16.323Z", "t_ms": 8734, "delta": "-hop QA) and Fever (fact verification) using PaLM-540B, ReAct outperformed action-only baselines and reduced"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 8.927, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 47, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:16.461Z", "t_ms": 8872, "delta": " hallucination rates compared to CoT [C1, C4, C5]. Combining ReAct with CoT self-consistency (Co"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.31, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 48, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:16.674Z", "t_ms": 9085, "delta": "T-SC) achieved the strongest overall prompting performance [C4, C6]. When fine-tuned on HotpotQA, smaller models ("}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 9.321, "data": {"request_id": "a39660b6dcb7", "seq": 49, "ts": "2026-10-28T05:04:16.857Z", "t_ms": 9268, "delta": "PaLM-8B and 62B) with ReAct outperformed larger prompting baselines [C6].\n* **Interactive Decision"}}
